# One-digit version raise

Every AmL product **and** every App Builder user project uses one digit (0–9)
in patch and in minor. Never write a two-digit patch or minor.

## Sequence

```
1.0.8 → 1.0.9 → 1.1.0 → 1.1.1 → … → 1.1.9 → 1.2.0
1.9.9 → 2.0.0
```

## Forbidden

```
❌ 1.0.9 → 1.0.10
❌ 1.0.11
❌ 1.10.0
```

## Agent rules

- Never bump patch past 9. Roll to the next minor, patch `0`.
- Never bump minor past 9. Roll to the next major, minor `0`, patch `0`.
- If a version is already two-digit (`1.0.10`, `1.0.11`), the next bump is
  `1.1.0`, not `1.0.12`.
- Do not invent `1.0.10` in changelogs, OTA labels, pubspec, or `version`.
- Copy this file into every new AmL app as `.cursor/rules/one-digit-version.mdc`
  with `alwaysApply: true`.
